---
title: Low-to-High Cable Flyes
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![сведение рук в кроссовере снизу](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/09937a69-3904-44ad-9af8-c7e99021fcf9)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Attach single handles to the low pulleys on both sides of the cable machine and grab them.

### Step 2
Stand in the center of the machine and take one step forward to create tension on the cables. Let your arms hang down and slightly back at your sides.

### Step 3
Keep a slight, fixed bend in your elbows throughout the entire set.

### Step 4
Exhale and bring your hands up and together in an upward arc until they reach upper-chest level, with your palms facing up toward the ceiling.

### Step 5
Squeeze your upper chest muscles firmly and hold for one second at the top of the movement.

### Step 6
Inhale and slowly lower your arms back down along the same path to the starting position, then immediately begin the next rep without pausing.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Do not perform this movement with locked-out, completely straight arms—keep a slight bend to protect your elbow joints.

• Bringing your hands higher and closer together at the top maximizes the contraction in your upper chest.

• This exercise effectively works the upper chest along with supporting chest muscles.

• Keep your torso upright and your elbow angle fixed—avoid bending your arms like a curl or leaning forward as you lift the handles.
{{< /callout >}}
